<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Runs `tmux-agents --sync` every 5s, so the agent-state glyph on a WezTerm tab
  stops being wrong in the three cases no Claude Code hook reports: a permission
  prompt being answered, a dialog dismissed, and a turn interrupted. See
  root/.claude/hooks/agent-state.md.

  WHY A POLLER AT ALL, given this repo's pane options were designed precisely to
  avoid polling. The options are cheap to READ -- a tmux format reads them with
  no subprocess, which is what keeps status-interval at 30s -- and nothing about
  that changes here. What is polled is the *source*: Claude Code publishes those
  three transitions to no hook, and `claude agents --json` is the documented way
  to read the state they leave behind. There is no event to subscribe to.

  WHY 5 SECONDS. The cost of a tick is one `tmux list-panes` plus, only when
  some pane is bound to a session, ~120ms of `claude agents --json` (measured).
  With no Claude running under tmux a tick is the list-panes and nothing else,
  so the machine pays for this only while it is in use. 5s is the dial between
  how long a stale 🛑 survives and how much of a core that costs while you have
  sessions open -- roughly 2.4% of one, at this interval. Raising it is safe;
  the only consequence is a slower correction.

  It writes nothing when the CLI agrees with the panes, which is the ordinary
  case: no tmux writes, no redraw, and not even a process per pane.

  The PATH and `sh -c` notes in com.ebkn.pr-review-watch.plist apply verbatim: a
  launchd agent inherits none of the login shell's environment. `claude` must be
  reachable on that PATH, and $HOME/.local/bin is where these dotfiles link it.

  Load with:  launchctl bootstrap gui/$UID ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.ebkn.tmux-agent-sync.plist
  Status:     launchctl print gui/$UID/com.ebkn.tmux-agent-sync
  Unload:     launchctl bootout gui/$UID/com.ebkn.tmux-agent-sync
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.ebkn.tmux-agent-sync</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/bin/sh</string>
        <string>-c</string>
        <string>exec env PATH="$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH" "$HOME/.local/bin/tmux-agents" --sync</string>
    </array>

    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <key>PATH</key>
        <string>/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
    </dict>

    <key>StartInterval</key>
    <integer>5</integer>

    <!-- StartInterval alone does NOT give 5s. launchd also refuses to spawn a
         job sooner than ThrottleInterval after its previous spawn, and that
         defaults to 10s (`launchctl print` shows it as "minimum runtime"), so
         this agent ran every 10s while everything here said 5. The interval is
         the pair of keys, and both have to change together. -->
    <key>ThrottleInterval</key>
    <integer>5</integer>

    <!-- Nothing is owed at login: there is no tmux server yet, so the first
         tick would do nothing but start a process. -->
    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <false/>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/tmp/tmux-agent-sync.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/tmp/tmux-agent-sync.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
